+   goal, done definition, authority envelope, delivery topology, ceilings,
+   model/reasoning policy, operator gates, and stop conditions before dispatch.
+2. Maintain the coordinator-owned program, approval, verification, review, and
+   integration ledgers. Existing planning, implementation, review, approval,
+   and verification contracts remain authoritative for every child.
+3. Use fresh user-visible Codex desktop tasks rather than subagents. Keep one
+   implementation writer in V0; read-only tasks may run only within the
+   operator-confirmed ceiling. Worktree-parallel implementation remains off.
+4. Reconcile task handles and evidence, fence stale assignments and leases,
+   reuse the original reviewer for re-review, recover bounded stalls, and keep
+   safe critical-path work moving after informational operator exchanges.
+5. Stop only at the furthest authorized done state, an explicit operator gate
+   or pause, a directional/credential conflict, or a genuine exhausted blocker.
+   Pushes, PRs, provider/live/paid/destructive work, and activation changes keep
+   their existing per-action approval requirements.
